                <pb facs="0098" n="86" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg86"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/16267a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Finland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Schoenfeld</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-10-30T19:00:00-05:00">October 30, 1941—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>223. Please see Ryti immediately and say that because of the rapidity with which
                    events seem to be moving we greatly desire to have a reply to your
                    representations of October 27 at the earliest possible moment and that in
                    pressing him in this regard we sincerely believe we are acting in Finland’s own
                    vital interest, for it is anticipated that by giving a delayed and unresponsive
                    reply to those representations, the Finnish Government will be weakening
                    immeasurably the hands of those of us who are still striving with great
                    difficulty to canalize developments in so far as possible along lines which
                    under foreseeable circumstances will best serve to protect Finnish interests in
                    the future.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
